 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Titanic Data Analysis with Pandas\n",
    "### Data Understanding, Preparation, and Passenger Survival Analysis\n",
    "\n"
   ],
   "id": "titanic-000"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 1) Project Brief\n",
    "\n",
    "The objective is to understand which passenger characteristics are associated with survival in the supplied Titanic sample. We examine sex, passenger class, age, fare, embarkation port, recorded family members, cabin information, and shared tickets.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is exploratory analysis, not a machine-learning prediction project. The outcome is `Survived`: **0 = did not survive**, **1 = survived**. All findings describe this sample of passengers."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-001"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1.1) Import Libraries\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objective:** Prepare data manipulation and visualization libraries."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-002"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "pd.set_option(\"display.max_columns\", None)\n",
    "pd.set_option(\"display.float_format\", \"{:,.2f}\".format)\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": 1,
   "outputs": [],
   "id": "titanic-003"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "Pandas handles tables, NumPy provides numerical utilities, and Matplotlib/Seaborn produce the charts. Formatting changes only how numbers are displayed, not the stored values."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-004"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1.2) Load the Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objective:** Load the supplied data while retaining an untouched raw copy."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-005"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "df_raw = pd.read_csv("titanic_dataset.csv")\n",
    "df = df_raw.copy()\n",
    "print(\"Shape:\", df.shape)"
   ],
   "execution_count": 2,
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "Dataset loaded successfully\n",
      "Shape: (891, 12)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "id": "titanic-006"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "The supplied CSV contains 891 rows and 12 columns. `df_raw` is the original source; `df` is used for inspection. The filename is explicit and easy to edit, as in the reference notebook."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-007"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 2) Data Understanding\n",
    "\n",
    "### Column Dictionary\n",
    "\n",
    "| Column | Meaning | Analytical role |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| PassengerId | Passenger identifier | Identifier |\n",
    "| Survived | 0 = did not survive; 1 = survived | Binary outcome |\n",
    "| Pclass | 1 = first; 2 = second; 3 = third class | Ordered category |\n",
    "| Name | Passenger full name | Text; can provide a title |\n",
    "| Sex | Recorded male/female category | Category |\n",
    "| Age | Age in years | Numerical; fractional ages represent infants |\n",
    "| SibSp | Siblings or spouses aboard | Numerical count |\n",
    "| Parch | Parents or children aboard | Numerical count |\n",
    "| Ticket | Ticket identifier | Identifier; useful for shared-ticket analysis |\n",
    "| Fare | Recorded ticket fare | Numerical |\n",
    "| Cabin | Recorded cabin number(s) | Text with substantial missingness |\n",
    "| Embarked | C = Cherbourg; Q = Queenstown; S = Southampton | Category |\n",
    "\n",
    "Each row represents **one passenger**, not one ticket or one family. Several passengers may share a ticket."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-008"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
