   "id": "titanic-038"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "Both counts are zero. No duplicate removal is needed. Repeated Ticket values should remain because distinct passengers can share a ticket."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-039"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3.3) Invalid Categories and Ranges\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objective:** Check whether coded categories or numerical values violate basic rules."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-040"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "validation = pd.Series({\n",
    "    \"Invalid Survived\": (~df[\"Survived\"].isin([0, 1])).sum(),\n",
    "    \"Invalid Pclass\": (~df[\"Pclass\"].isin([1, 2, 3])).sum(),\n",
    "    \"Invalid Sex\": (~df[\"Sex\"].isin([\"male\", \"female\"])).sum(),\n",
    "    \"Invalid known Embarked\": (~df[\"Embarked\"].dropna().isin([\"C\", \"Q\", \"S\"])).sum(),\n",
    "    \"Age outside 0 to 120\": ((df[\"Age\"] < 0) | (df[\"Age\"] > 120)).sum(),\n",
    "    \"Negative Fare\": (df[\"Fare\"] < 0).sum(),\n",
    "    \"Negative SibSp\": (df[\"SibSp\"] < 0).sum(),\n",
    "    \"Negative Parch\": (df[\"Parch\"] < 0).sum(),\n",
    "    \"Non-integer SibSp\": (df[\"SibSp\"] % 1 != 0).sum(),\n",
    "    \"Non-integer Parch\": (df[\"Parch\"] % 1 != 0).sum()\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "validation"
   ],
   "execution_count": 13,
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "Invalid Survived          0\n",
      "Invalid Pclass            0\n",
      "Invalid Sex               0\n",
      "Invalid known Embarked    0\n",
      "Age outside 0 to 120      0\n",
      "Negative Fare             0\n",
      "Negative SibSp            0\n",
      "Negative Parch            0\n",
      "Non-integer SibSp         0\n",
      "Non-integer Parch         0\n",
      "dtype: int64\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "id": "titanic-041"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "All checks return zero for this dataset. This confirms basic plausibility, not complete historical accuracy. Fractional ages are valid; fares of zero require context but are not negative fares."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-042"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3.4) Statistical Outlier Review\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objective:** Flag unusual Age, Fare, SibSp and Parch values without deleting them."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-043"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "outlier_rows = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for col in [\"Age\", \"Fare\", \"SibSp\", \"Parch\"]:\n",
    "    q1 = df[col].quantile(0.25)\n",
    "    q3 = df[col].quantile(0.75)\n",
    "    iqr = q3 - q1\n",
    "    lower_limit = q1 - 1.5 * iqr\n",
    "    upper_limit = q3 + 1.5 * iqr\n",
    "    flagged = df[(df[col] < lower_limit) | (df[col] > upper_limit)]\n",
    "\n",
    "    outlier_rows.append({\n",
    "        \"Column\": col,\n",
    "        \"Minimum\": df[col].min(),\n",
    "        \"Maximum\": df[col].max(),\n",
    "        \"Lower_Limit\": lower_limit,\n",
    "        \"Upper_Limit\": upper_limit,\n",
    "        \"Flagged_Rows\": len(flagged)\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "pd.DataFrame(outlier_rows)"
   ],
   "execution_count": 14,
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "  Column  Minimum  Maximum  Lower_Limit  Upper_Limit  Flagged_Rows\n",
      "0    Age     0.42    80.00        -6.69        64.81            11\n",
      "1   Fare     0.00   512.33       -26.72        65.63           116\n",
      "2  SibSp     0.00     8.00        -1.50         2.50            46\n",
      "3  Parch     0.00     6.00         0.00         0.00           213\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "id": "titanic-044"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Code Explanation\n",
    "\n",
    "`quantile(0.25)` and `quantile(0.75)` define the central 50% of values. IQR is their difference. The 1.5×IQR bounds are statistical flags, not proof of incorrect data."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-045"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "The IQR rule flags 11 ages, 116 fares, 46 SibSp values and 213 Parch values. Count variables can have zero IQR because most observations are zero, so their flags are especially unsuitable as deletion rules. All plausible records remain."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-046"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
