    "High fares occur in first class, and identical fares can occur for passengers sharing a ticket. This supports retaining them while interpreting Fare cautiously."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-049"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 4) Data Preparation and Feature Engineering\n",
    "\n",
    "### Preparation Decisions\n",
    "\n",
    "| Field / issue | Decision | Reason |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Raw data | Preserve `df_raw` | Keep the source available for comparison |\n",
    "| Age | Retain missing values | Avoid inventing ages for age-specific findings |\n",
    "| Embarked | Label missing values Unknown | Keep passengers without guessing a port |\n",
    "| Cabin | Retain text and create availability indicator | Missingness is extensive and informative |\n",
    "| Outliers | Retain plausible values | Extreme fares and family counts need not be errors |\n",
    "| PassengerId / Ticket / Name | Retain, but exclude identifiers from correlation | Identifier numbers are not meaningful continuous measures |\n",
    "\n",
    "No rows are dropped from the main dataset. A separate `df_age` contains only passengers with recorded ages for age-specific comparisons."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-050"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4.1) Create the Prepared Copy\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objective:** Apply the justified missing-port treatment."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-051"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "df_clean = df.copy()\n",
    "df_clean[\"Embarked\"] = df_clean[\"Embarked\"].fillna(\"Unknown\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Rows after preparation:\", len(df_clean))\n",
    "print(\"Missing ages retained:\", df_clean[\"Age\"].isna().sum())"
   ],
   "execution_count": 16,
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "Rows after preparation: 891\n",
      "Missing ages retained: 177\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "id": "titanic-052"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "All 891 passengers remain. The two unknown ports receive a label for grouped reporting, while the 177 unknown ages remain missing."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-053"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4.2) Readable Outcome and Class Labels\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objective:** Map coded fields to readable labels without replacing the originals."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-054"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "survival_map = {0: \"Did Not Survive\", 1: \"Survived\"}\n",
    "class_map = {1: \"First\", 2: \"Second\", 3: \"Third\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "df_clean[\"Survival_Status\"] = df_clean[\"Survived\"].map(survival_map)\n",
    "df_clean[\"Class_Name\"] = df_clean[\"Pclass\"].map(class_map)\n",
    "\n",
    "df_clean[[\"Survived\", \"Survival_Status\", \"Pclass\", \"Class_Name\"]].head()"
   ],
   "execution_count": 17,
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "   Survived  Survival_Status  Pclass Class_Name\n",
      "0         0  Did Not Survive       3      Third\n",
      "1         1         Survived       1      First\n",
      "2         1         Survived       3      Third\n",
      "3         1         Survived       1      First\n",
      "4         0  Did Not Survive       3      Third\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "id": "titanic-055"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "`map()` translates values using a dictionary, as in the reference notebook. Keeping the original Survived column lets us calculate survival rates from 0/1 values."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-056"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4.3) Family Size and Alone Status\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objective:** Measure recorded relatives and identify passengers without them."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-057"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "df_clean[\"FamilySize\"] = df_clean[\"SibSp\"] + df_clean[\"Parch\"] + 1\n",
    "\n",
    "df_clean[\"Travel_Group\"] = \"With recorded family\"\n",
    "df_clean.loc[df_clean[\"FamilySize\"] == 1, \"Travel_Group\"] = \"Alone\"\n",
    "\n",
    "df_clean[[\"SibSp\", \"Parch\", \"FamilySize\", \"Travel_Group\"]].head()"
   ],
   "execution_count": 18,
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "   SibSp  Parch  FamilySize          Travel_Group\n",
      "0      1      0           2  With recorded family\n",
      "1      1      0           2  With recorded family\n",
      "2      0      0           1                 Alone\n",
      "3      1      0           2  With recorded family\n",
      "4      0      0           1                 Alone\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "id": "titanic-058"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "The +1 includes the passenger. Alone means no recorded siblings/spouses or parents/children aboard; the passenger may still have travelled with friends or others. `loc` assigns a value only to rows satisfying the condition."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-059"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4.4) Age Groups and Children\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objective:** Define age bins and a documented child threshold."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-060"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "age_bins = [0, 16, 30, 45, 60, np.inf]\n",
    "age_labels = [\"0-15\", \"16-29\", \"30-44\", \"45-59\", \"60+\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "df_clean[\"AgeGroup\"] = pd.cut(\n",
    "    df_clean[\"Age\"], bins=age_bins, labels=age_labels, right=False\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "df_clean[\"Age_Category\"] = \"Unknown\"\n",
    "df_clean.loc[df_clean[\"Age\"] < 16, \"Age_Category\"] = \"Child (<16)\"\n",
    "df_clean.loc[df_clean[\"Age\"] >= 16, \"Age_Category\"] = \"Adult (16+)\"\n",
    "\n",
    "df_age = df_clean.dropna(subset=[\"Age\"]).copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Passengers with recorded ages:\", len(df_age))\n",
    "print(df_clean[\"Age_Category\"].value_counts())"
   ],
   "execution_count": 19,
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "Passengers with recorded ages: 714\n",
      "Age_Category\n",
      "Adult (16+)    631\n",
      "Unknown        177\n",
      "Child (<16)     83\n",
      "Name: count, dtype: int64\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "id": "titanic-061"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Code Explanation\n",
    "\n",
    "`pd.cut()` uses explicit boundaries. With `right=False`, 16 belongs to 16–29, 30 to 30–44, 45 to 45–59, and 60 to 60+. Fractional ages remain in the correct interval. These labels are age ranges, not rounded individual ages. Missing ages remain missing in AgeGroup."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-062"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "There are 83 children under 16, 631 adults with known ages, and 177 passengers with unknown ages. The 714-row `df_age` is used only for age-specific summaries."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-063"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4.5) Fare Quartiles\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objective:** Create sample-relative fare groups for rate comparison."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-064"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "fare_labels = [\"Q1 Lowest\", \"Q2\", \"Q3\", \"Q4 Highest\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "df_clean[\"FareGroup\"] = pd.qcut(\n",
    "    df_clean[\"Fare\"], q=4, labels=fare_labels\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Fare quartile boundaries:\")\n",
    "print(df_clean[\"Fare\"].quantile([0, 0.25, 0.50, 0.75, 1]))\n",
    "print(\"\\nPassengers per group:\")\n",
    "print(df_clean[\"FareGroup\"].value_counts(sort=False))"
   ],
   "execution_count": 20,
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "Fare quartile boundaries:\n",
      "0.00     0.00\n",
      "0.25     7.91\n",
      "0.50    14.45\n",
      "0.75    31.00\n",
      "1.00   512.33\n",
      "Name: Fare, dtype: float64\n",
      "\n",
      "Passengers per group:\n",
      "FareGroup\n",
      "Q1 Lowest     223\n",
      "Q2            224\n",
      "Q3            222\n",
      "Q4 Highest    222\n",
      "Name: count, dtype: int64\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "id": "titanic-065"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Code Explanation\n",
    "\n",
    "`cut()` uses chosen numerical intervals; `qcut()` uses sample quantiles to form groups of approximately equal size. Q4 is the highest quarter of recorded fares in this sample, not an official ticket category."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-066"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "The boundaries are approximately 0, 7.91, 14.45, 31.00 and 512.33. Equal fares at a boundary can produce slightly unequal group sizes."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-067"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4.6) Cabin Information\n",
