  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 6) Passenger Survival Analysis — All 30 Questions\n",
    "\n",
    "### How to Read a Survival Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "- `Passengers`: number of passenger records in the group.\n",
    "- `Survivors`: sum of the 0/1 Survived values.\n",
    "- `Survival_Pct`: mean of Survived multiplied by 100.\n",
    "\n",
    "For example, values `[1, 0, 1, 0]` have mean 0.5, meaning 50% survival. We show both rates and counts because a high percentage based on two passengers has much less support than a similar percentage based on hundreds.\n",
    "\n",
    "The code remains explicit in each question so the calculations are visible. For categorical groupings, `observed=True` includes categories present in the data instead of manufacturing empty category combinations. Age analyses use `df_age`, whose 714 passengers have recorded ages."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-094"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q1) Overall Passenger Survival Rate\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objective:** Calculate survival for the full sample."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-095"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "total_passengers = len(df_clean)\n",
    "total_survivors = df_clean[\"Survived\"].sum()\n",
    "overall_survival_pct = total_survivors / total_passengers * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Passengers:\", total_passengers)\n",
    "print(\"Survivors:\", total_survivors)\n",
    "print(\"Did not survive:\", total_passengers - total_survivors)\n",
    "print(\"Survival percentage:\", round(overall_survival_pct, 2))"
   ],
   "execution_count": 29,
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "Passengers: 891\n",
      "Survivors: 342\n",
      "Did not survive: 549\n",
      "Survival percentage: 38.38\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "id": "titanic-096"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "342 of 891 passengers survived: **38.38%**. The remaining 549 did not survive. This is the baseline for later group comparisons."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-097"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q2) Survival by Sex\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objective:** Compare male and female passenger outcomes."
   ],
   "id": "titanic-098"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "survival_by_sex = (\n",
    "    df_clean.groupby('Sex', as_index=False, observed=True)\n",
    "    .agg(\n",
    "        Passengers=(\"Survived\", \"size\"),\n",
    "        Survivors=(\"Survived\", \"sum\"),\n",
    "        Survival_Rate=(\"Survived\", \"mean\")\n",
    "    )\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "survival_by_sex[\"Survival_Pct\"] = survival_by_sex[\"Survival_Rate\"] * 100\n",
    "survival_by_sex = survival_by_sex.drop(columns=[\"Survival_Rate\"])\n",
    "survival_by_sex"
   ],
   "execution_count": 30,
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "      Sex  Passengers  Survivors  Survival_Pct\n",
      "0  female         314        233         74.20\n",
      "1    male         577        109         18.89\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "id": "titanic-099"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "Females survived at **74.20%** (233/314), versus **18.89%** (109/577) for males. This large descriptive association will be checked within passenger classes in Q12."
   ],
